From a01b030c3d844033c895d04e64fffc29fcd0b9c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:30:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Give each KV cache group its own blocks in every dummy layout

The DeepSeek V4 attention profile runs a full-budget prefill on a minimal
cache of one block, which every KV cache group then used at once. The
groups overlay the same memory, so at TP3 the drafter's sliding window
read the target's records in its own format and its first attention
returned non-finite rows, which TileKernels' fused gate refuses.

assign_dummy_blocks gives each group its own slice of the pool after the
null block, and each request of a group its own blocks within the slice,
wrapping inside the slice when it runs out. set_dummy_context and the
attention profile both use it, and the attention profile allocates one
block per group.
